WHAT SHIPS WITH A PAID KEY

Provider fallback. When a provider goes down, your request re-routes to ano=
ther provider serving the same model. No retry logic on your end, no downti=
me for your users. Prompt caching. Repeated context gets cached on supporte=
d models. Cuts repeated-context cost by up to 90%.

=E2=80=83

AND MORE

Model variants. Append :nitro for speed, :floor for the cheapest provider, =
or :exacto for precision routing. Same model, different optimization, one s=
tring change. Dedicated rate limits. Free-tier keys share a pool. Paid keys=
 get their own limits, so other users' traffic never touches yours. No dail=
y request cap. Free tier limits you to 10 requests per day. Paid keys have =
no ceiling.

How pricing works. No provider markup. You pay the per-token rate each prov=
ider sets. The activity dashboard ( https://openrouter.ai/activity?utm_sour=
ce=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm_content=
